From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a virtual GPU draws the pointer where clicks land

The DRM cursor was set with drmModeSetCursor, which carries no hotspot.
A virtual GPU (vmwgfx, virtio-gpu, qxl) hands the cursor image to its
host, which draws it at the host's pointer by that hotspot, so with 0,0
an arrow's tip was drawn 6,4 px up and left of where clicks landed.

The host now sends each cursor's hotspot to the GPU process with its
bitmaps, and every CRTC sets it with drmModeSetCursor2. The cursor is
still placed by its image's top left. Chromium sets the cursor through
the legacy ioctls only, never as an atomic plane, so the atomic HOTSPOT
properties have nothing to carry.
